title: Authorizations › New Case › Authorization preparation › An agent asks a question
route: /authorizations/new/:draftId (step 4 of 5, the question pop-up)
intro: Scribe (or Packet) stops to ask what the chart cannot say, and the agents wait. A run has one question, or two when the chart leaves a gap, and the pop-up says 'Question 1 of N' with the true N. A question cannot be skipped: 'Answer later' only closes the pop-up. Each answer goes into the draft and into the summary.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "The run reaches Scribe\n(Packet for IOP and PHP)"
process p1 "The agent works about 45% of its step, then stops"
decision dKey "Which questions were planned when the agents started?\nThe first one is asked now, a second right after the first answer"
process q1 "Sertraline\n'Sertraline starts 9/14 on the medication list and 9/21 in the psychiatric evaluation. Which is right?'\nChoices: '9/14 (the medication list)', '9/21 (the psychiatric evaluation)'"
process q2 "Step-down provider\n'Is a named step-down provider on file? Summit asks for one in residential continued stays.'\nChoices: 'Yes, a named provider is on file', 'Not yet. One will be named before day 10', 'Not applicable for this request'"
process q4 "Diagnosis duration (Scribe)\n'How long has the patient had this diagnosis? The psychiatric evaluation is not in the case, so Scribe cannot read it from there.'\nChoices: 'Less than a year', 'One to five years', 'More than five years'"
process q5 "Why a lower level is not enough (Scribe)\n'Why is a lower level of care not enough? The chart does not say, and the payer will ask.'\nChoices: 'A lower level was tried and did not hold', 'Home is not safe or supportive enough', 'Symptoms are too severe for a lower level'"
process q3 "Discharge date (Packet)\n'Is a discharge or step-down date planned in the next 30 days? The payer's form asks for it.'\nChoices: 'Yes, within 2 weeks', 'Yes, within 30 days', 'Not decided yet'"
screen sc "Step 4 shows the question\nThe asking row: 'Needs your answer' and a button 'Answer'\nGreen card: 'Question 1 of 2 from Scribe.' and the text\nNo banner shows while the question is open\nHint: 'The agents are waiting for your answer.'"
overlay oM "Scribe has a question\n'Question 1 of 2 for this case. The agents wait for you.'\nChoice cards, then 'Or add a note in your own words'"
process pNoSkip "'Pause all agents' and 'Skip ahead' do not get past the question"

input iChoice "Click one choice card\nIt highlights"
input iNote "Type a note\n'Optional with a button above, or use it on its own.'"
decision dReady "A choice or a note given?"
process pOff "'Send answer' stays switched off"
click cSend "Click 'Send answer'"
store stAns "Answer saved on the draft\nThe choice's words without the bracket, or the typed note\nA note typed with a choice is kept beside it"
store stClear "The summary draft is cleared so Scribe rebuilds it"
toast tYou "'You answered Scribe: ANSWER. It is in the draft.'\nWith a typed note: 'ANSWER · NOTE. It is in the draft.'"
decision dMore "Is a second question planned for this agent?"
agent aGo "The agent finishes the other 55% of its step\nThen the remaining agents run"
process pEffect "Sertraline answer: the Medication list finding becomes 'Sertraline start date confirmed by you: 9/14'\nStep-down 'Yes': the tick-box 'Name the step-down provider' disappears\nA duration or lower-level answer becomes a sentence in the summary"
process pSum "The draft summary uses the answer\nClinical picture: 'Sertraline was started on 9/14.'\nPlan: 'A named step-down provider is on file.'"

click cLater "Click 'Answer later', press Escape, or click outside"
process pLater "Pop-up closes; the agents stay stopped\nBanner stays; the row keeps 'Needs your answer'"
click cAnswer "Click 'Answer' on the agent's row"
process pLeave "Leave and come back: the pop-up opens again by itself"
goto gCM "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Being prepared card"
goto g36 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › Authorization preparation › Finished, paused or left"

s1 --> p1 --> dKey
dKey -->|Medication list has the sertraline finding| q1
dKey -->|Residential 3.5 or Detox| q2
dKey -->|IOP or PHP| q3
dKey -->|Second question: no psychiatric evaluation in the case| q4
dKey -->|Second question: no psychosocial, treatment plan, ASAM or nursing document for the level of care, or no reason| q5
q1 --> sc
q2 --> sc
q3 --> sc
q4 --> sc
q5 --> sc
sc --> oM --> pNoSkip
oM --> iChoice --> dReady
oM --> iNote --> dReady
dReady -->|No| pOff --> iChoice
dReady -->|Yes| cSend --> stAns --> stClear --> tYou --> dMore
dMore -->|Yes| p1
dMore -->|No| aGo --> pEffect --> pSum --> g36
oM --> cLater --> pLater --> cAnswer --> oM
pLater --> pLeave --> oM
sc --> gCM
